From b61f45007600437a492496fd7f1067f2ac97c08b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 14:42:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Clients icon: hand-built colored badge instead of DiceBear;
 revert square avatar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The DiceBear `icons` style gamble didn't land (network policy here
blocks api.dicebear.com, so the previous commit's seed was never
actually previewed before shipping). Replaced it with a plain,
hand-built badge instead: a solid rounded-square in the app's own brand
color with a white Users glyph centered in it — same macOS-app-icon
look the user wants, fully visible in the code instead of hidden behind
an opaque seed hash.

Also reverts the MW avatar's border-radius removal from the previous
commit — square initials avatar goes back to its normal rounded corners
in the active-client pill. Dropped the now-unused `square` prop off
ClientAvatar and the `radius` option off generateInitialsAvatarDataUri
entirely rather than leaving dead capability behind.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011PX9qLTKPtXba6ncjAwLyN
